  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the region $R=\\left\\{(x, y): x \\leq y \\leq 9-\\frac{11}{3} x^2, x \\geq 0\\right\\}$.\nThe area, of the largest rectangle of sides parallel to the coordinate axes and inscribed in R , is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "LR626",
      "text": "$\\frac{730}{119}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "xpTA5",
      "text": "$\\frac{625}{111}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RgpaA",
      "text": "$\\frac{821}{123}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4JaM5",
      "text": "$\\frac{567}{121}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{t} .\\left(9-\\frac{11 \\mathrm{t}^2}{3}-\\mathrm{t}\\right)$\n\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/-fmqPBqYEjxt2mXhKwMGuC7U2efZQrQN66p2Rn2jo0o.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{A}=9 \\mathrm{t}-\\mathrm{t}^2-\\frac{11}{3} \\mathrm{t}^3 \\\\ & \\frac{\\mathrm{dA}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=9-2 \\mathrm{t}-11 \\mathrm{t}^2 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 11 \\mathrm{t}^2+2 \\mathrm{t}-9=0 \\\\ & 11 \\mathrm{t}^2+11 \\mathrm{t}-9 \\mathrm{t}-9=0 \\\\ & \\mathrm{t}=-1 \\& \\mathrm{t}=\\frac{9}{11}\\end{aligned}$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/BStwGSccrW__mRzM8nKCdyUIMC3cNJ0aqQ6HtCVh6zs.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\therefore \\text { largest area }=\\frac{9}{11}\\left(9-\\frac{11}{3}, \\frac{81}{121}-\\frac{9}{11}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{9}{11} \\cdot \\frac{63}{11}=\\frac{567}{121}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
